From 53d476c0f1ead618b15288f1cd78b69e2a1c4d67 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 05:15:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] name residual sync-round steps and pin empty-probe
 boundaries

The perpetual sync worker now books round residuals, but the historical
13.39065ms non-board overhead cannot be allocated from its aggregate counters.
Name completed discovery, sweep, selection, deferred/backlog, after-round,
report and wait work using existing residual scoped_call accounting. Nested
board CPU stays accounted once; disabled scopes preserve the direct call.

Extend the empty-outbox cut's controls for rejected-to-pending transitions,
closed observers, and fresh awake verdicts. Main-file mtime/size changes reopen
the observer to prevent equal-header restore reuse. This deliberately also
invalidates generations on checkpoint; ordinary WAL commits retain generation.
Trace replacement DELETE-mode handles and isolate the existing burst-write
window test from autocheckpoint, retaining all deadline assertions and adding
an explicit checkpoint invalidation control.

Proof: behavioral RED missing step names; GREEN 109 tests in 8 focused files.
Six exact-anchor mutants killed with named tests. Full 210-file consumer run
exposed the two checkpoint/trace fixture assumptions; both corrected without
weakening deadline/output assertions, final focused suites and full check pass.
Collector synthetic controls separately cover observation brackets, stale/busy
reads, PID/code mismatch, ancestry binding and negative-residual rejection.
No Mac performance acceptance claimed; independent exact-head CI/review and
one naturally deployed mature-idle measurement remain mandatory.
